  "summary": "An agitated (stirred-tank) reactor mixes reactants in a vessel with a motor-driven agitator. Wall baffles stop the liquid simply swirling and turn the flow into top-to-bottom circulation. A jacket and/or internal coil add or remove the reaction heat. It is the workhorse of batch chemical and pharmaceutical production.",
